 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p><b>JSP (JavaServer Pages)</b> is a server-side technology to create dynamic web pages by writing Java code inside HTML. Every JSP is converted into a servlet by the container.</p><h3>Features</h3><ul><li>Easy to write the view (HTML) part.</li><li>Automatic compilation; changes do not need manual redeploy.</li><li>Implicit objects (request, response, session, out…).</li><li>Supports tags, JSTL and JavaBeans (&lt;jsp:useBean&gt;).</li></ul><h3>JSP life cycle</h3><pre>hello.jsp → (translate) → hello_jsp.java → (compile) → .class → jspInit() → _jspService() per request → jspDestroy()</pre>",
 "quiz": {
  "q": "What does the container turn a JSP into?",
